@startuml Timetable Change Saga — Choreography with RabbitMQ

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequenceBoxBorderColor #444
skinparam noteBorderColor #888

title Timetable Change Saga (Saga Choreography Pattern)

actor      "Admin"                   as A
participant "RoutingService\n:9999"  as R  #LightBlue
queue      "RabbitMQ\ntimetable.exchange" as Q  #Orange
participant "NotificationService\n:8086" as N  #LightYellow

== Happy Path ==

A -> R : PUT /api/v1/lines/{id}\n(or /directions/{id} or /timetables/{id})
activate R

R -> R : **Local TX**\nUpdate Line/Direction/Timetable in DB\ngenerate sagaId

R -> Q : **timetable.changed**\n{sagaId, lineId, lineCode, lineName, changeType}
R --> A : 200 OK {updated entity}
deactivate R

Q -> N : timetable.changed
activate N

N -> N : **Local TX**\nfetch active subscribers for lineId\nbulk-create Notification rows (TIMETABLE_CHANGE)

N -> Q : **timetable.notification.sent**\n{sagaId, lineId, notifiedCount}
deactivate N

Q -> R : timetable.notification.sent
activate R
R -> R : log "Saga [sagaId]: notifications sent\nto N subscribers for line X"\n**SAGA FINALIZED ✓**
deactivate R

== Compensation Path (NotificationService fails) ==

|||
A -> R : PUT /api/v1/lines/{id}
activate R
R -> R : **Local TX**\nUpdate entity in DB\ngenerate sagaId
R -> Q : **timetable.changed**\n{sagaId, lineId, ...}
R --> A : 200 OK
deactivate R

Q -> N : timetable.changed
activate N
N -> N : broadcast() — FAILS\n(DB error / exception)\nnotifications NOT created
N -> Q : **timetable.notification.failed**\n{sagaId, lineId, reason}
deactivate N

Q -> R : timetable.notification.failed
activate R
R -> R : log warning\n**Compensating action:**\nrepublish timetable.changed (RETRY)
R -> Q : **timetable.changed** {sagaId, changeType="RETRY"}
deactivate R

note over R, N
  RoutingService DB write is always committed regardless of notification outcome.
  Compensation retries notification delivery once — further retries left to ops.
end note

@enduml
